Hi All,
I am trying to use pcount to model bird abundances using some
variable-width transect counts in forest.  To deal with some low
detectability species I have aggregated (summed) counts from points
clustered within sites (typically transects separated by 200m in
clusters of 3 to 6).  As different total numbers of points per cluster
were sampled on each visits, I have tried to add an area offset
consisting of the log of the sum of the transect distances walked per
visit. My model looks like this:

pcount(formula = ~wet + season + temp_anomaly + month +
offset(log(distance)) ~ MATemp + MATemp2 + aspect + annual_pptn12 +
     time_step3 + MATemp.time_step3 + MATemp2.time_step3, data = spp.umf,
