Dear all,

since Murray's more mechanistic model for detection as a function of time duration cannot currently be fitted in unmarked, I was wondering how to best approximate this as a linear function of time or of a function of time (e.g., the log). The attached code does this. I think I would simply try a linear, quadratic and possibly cubic polynomial of time or possibly log(time).

Kind regards  --  Marc

P <- function(ts, t0, lambda0){ 1 - exp(-ts/t0 * lambda0)}
ts <- 1:100
t0 <- 1
lambda0 <- 0.01

for(lambda0 in c(0.001, 0.01, 0.1, 1, 2, 4, 6)){
par(mfrow = c(1,2))
plot(ts, P(ts, t0, lambda0), xlab = "Duration", ylab = "Detection probability",
   main = paste("lambda0:", lambda0), ylim = c(0,1), type = "l")
plot(log(ts), P(ts, t0, lambda0), xlab = "log(Duration)", ylab = "Detection probability",
   main = paste("lambda0:", lambda0), ylim = c(0,1), type = "l")
browser()
}

