Hi all,
I am working on modeling some multi-species population changes in forest birds, through time and across environmental gradients using pcount().  I also have information on effective strip width estimated from a subset of distance sampling surveys and gdistsamp().  My question: Is it valid to use these effective strip widths as a multiplier to convert my abundances from pcount() into absolute densities, or does this somehow duplicate the detection modelling?  Would maximum detection distance be appropriate? any thoughts would be much appreciated
Alex

