What I meant with a more complex model was something in BUGS where you estimate the distance sampling portion using your subset and then use those estimated parameters in the detection model for the full count data.  Obviously gdistsamp already does what you need regarding uncertainty in detection & availability (MRDS), but your specific problem relates to the fact that you don't have distance data for most of the sites/surveys.  Again though, it seems fine to me to use the ESW for establishing your effective sampling area for the plots in pcount.

